{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.peak_is_not_bulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.peak_is_not_bulk","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**The peak is not a bulk quantity — the interpretive punchline.** Whatever mass number maximises\nthe per-nucleon binding, its value is strictly below `a_V`, and the shortfall is precisely the\nsurface-plus-Coulomb cost at that point. Therefore a constant matching the observed peak matches an\ninterior maximum of a surface/Coulomb competition, not the bulk coefficient — the two differ by a\nparameter-dependent amount with no fundamental significance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_decreasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_decreasing","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L101-L115","doc":"**Falling branch.** Once the Coulomb cost dominates the surface cost\n(`a_C(u₁+u₂)u₁u₂ > a_S`), the per-nucleon binding DECREASES with mass number. Together with\n`perNucleon_increasing` this gives an interior maximum: the curve peaks and then declines, exactly as\nthe AME data do beyond A≈60. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L87-L99","doc":"**Rising branch.** While the Coulomb cost is small against the surface cost\n(`a_C(u₁+u₂)u₁u₂ < a_S`), the per-nucleon binding INCREASES with mass number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_sub","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L78-L85","doc":"The exact difference of the curve at two points — the algebraic engine for the rising and\nfalling branches below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_lt_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon_lt_volume","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L67-L76","doc":"**The curve never attains the bulk coefficient.** For a positive surface cost and a non-negative\nCoulomb cost, `f(u) < a_V` at every `u > 0` — so the observed maximum of the per-nucleon binding lies\nSTRICTLY BELOW `a_V`. This is the structural reason the empirical `B/A` peak is not the bulk\ncoefficient, and hence why matching a constant to that peak says nothing about the bulk. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.volume_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.volume_gap","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L62-L65","doc":"**The deficit from the bulk coefficient is exactly the surface-plus-Coulomb cost.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SaturationPeakStructure.perNucleon","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SaturationPeakStructure.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Per-nucleon binding in the volume−surface−Coulomb shape, in the variable `u = A^(1/3) > 0`:\n`f(u) = a_V − a_S/u − a_C·u²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}